From: axon7m bring-up
Subject: [PATCH] drm/crtc: no BUG when a CRTC fence signals during a name query

dma_fence_signal_locked() sets fence->ops to NULL for fences that have
neither release nor wait, which includes drm_crtc_fence_ops.
dma_fence_driver_name() checks "not signalled and ops set" and then calls
drm_crtc_fence_get_driver_name(); when the vblank interrupt signals the
fence on another CPU in between, fence_to_crtc() reads ops again, finds
NULL and hits its BUG_ON. Android's HWUI asks for fence names through
SYNC_IOC_FILE_INFO all the time: kernel panic in RenderThread
(drm_crtc.c:161, LineageOS 24 run 25, 2026-11-12). The CRTC is still
reachable through the fence's lock pointer, so only warn on a foreign ops.
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_crtc.c	2026-11-12 10:41:18.226999396 +0100
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_crtc.c	2026-11-12 10:41:18.296702973 +0100
@@ -158,7 +158,15 @@
 
 static struct drm_crtc *fence_to_crtc(struct dma_fence *fence)
 {
-	BUG_ON(rcu_access_pointer(fence->ops) != &drm_crtc_fence_ops);
+	const struct dma_fence_ops *ops = rcu_access_pointer(fence->ops);
+
+	/*
+	 * dma_fence_signal_locked() sets ops to NULL for fences without
+	 * release and wait, like these: a name query that saw the fence
+	 * unsignalled can get here after a vblank signalled it on another
+	 * CPU. The lock pointer is still the CRTC's.
+	 */
+	WARN_ON_ONCE(ops && ops != &drm_crtc_fence_ops);
 	return container_of(fence->extern_lock, struct drm_crtc, fence_lock);
 }
 
